
{"id":"ce0a8f87-b27e-49a0-be4d-dbe169c195dd","object":"chat.completion","created":1785029570,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    capacity = case['capacity']\\n    trials = case['trials']\\n    memory = []\\n    for i, trial in enumerate(trials):\\n        entry = {\\n            'last_trial': i,\\n            'reflection': trial['reflection'],\\n            'signature': trial['signature'],\\n            'success': trial['success']\\n        }\\n        if not entry['success']:\\n            for j, mem in enumerate(memory):\\n                if not mem['success'] and mem['signature'] == entry['signature']:\\n                    memory.pop(j)\\n                    break\\n        memory.append(entry)\\n    memory.sort(key=lambda x: x['last_trial'])\\n    if len(memory) > capacity:\\n        failures = [m for m in memory if not m['success']]\\n        successes = [m for m in memory if m['success']]\\n        failures.sort(key=lambda x: (-x['last_trial'], x['signature']))\\n        successes.sort(key=lambda x: (-x['last_trial'], x['signature']))\\n        combined = failures + successes\\n        truncated = combined[:capacity]\\n        truncated.sort(key=lambda x: x['last_trial'])\\n        memory = truncated\\n    signatures = [m['signature'] for m in memory]\\n    return {'memory': memory, 'signatures': signatures}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that processes the trials and maintains an episodic memory with capacity. The input case is a payload object with fields like \"capacity\" and \"trials\". The output must follow the given schema: object with \"memory\" (array of objects with last_trial, reflection, signature, success) and \"signatures\" (array of strings, presumably the signatures of retained memory entries, order same as memory).\n\nKey requirements from the task description:\n- Process trials in chronological order (order given)\